# The model pin for the comparison. One place, sent explicitly to every CLI call —
# never left to a CLI default, which drifts silently between runs.
#
# Tier check 2026-09-04. Names ending in "flash"/"mini"/"nano"/"luna" are a vendor's
# cheap/fast tier, not a neutral size label — check pricing/tier docs, not the name.
MODEL_CLAUDE="claude-haiku-4-5-20251001"    # cheap tier, chosen for price over mid-tier sonnet-5
MODEL_CODEX="gpt-5.6-terra"                 # mid tier. sol=flagship, luna=cheap (was wrongly set to luna)
MODEL_GROK="grok-4-3-direct"                # custom [model.grok-4-3-direct] in ~/.grok/config.toml, routed
                                             # to api.x.ai. grok's own session login only exposes grok-4.6
                                             # through cli-chat-proxy.grok.com (confirmed server-side).
                                             # REQUIRES: export XAI_API_KEY before running -- without it, grok
                                             # silently falls back to the session credential instead of erroring.
MODEL_KIMI="moonshotai/kimi-k2.7-code"      # needs the provider/ prefix, plain "kimi-k2.7-code" is rejected
MODEL_DEEPSEEK="deepseek-pro"                # reasonix takes its own provider name, not the raw DeepSeek model
                                             # id -- confirmed in ~/.reasonix/config.toml: provider "deepseek-pro"
                                             # wraps model "deepseek-v4-pro". Flagship, $1.32/$3.96 per M (peak
                                             # rate, current price list price), still cheaper output than every
                                             # mid-tier competitor except Kimi K2.7-Code.
MODEL_ANTIGRAVITY="gemini-3.6-flash"        # mid tier here -- confirmed 03-09-2026, Google's ladder is
                                             # Pro > Flash > Flash-Lite, so Flash is mid not cheap
ANTIGRAVITY_EFFORT="high"                    # agy requires --effort whenever --model is set
MODEL_COPILOT=""                            # no model pin possible -- confirmed 04-09-2026, every
                                             # --model choice ("gpt-5-mini", "claude-haiku-4.5", etc)
                                             # errors "not available" on this account/plan. Copilot CLI
                                             # always runs its own default, unpinned. Comparison caveat:
                                             # this run's model identity is whatever GitHub served that day.
